# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOURCE
#
# Every contraction below is taken from ڪامل سنڌي بريل درجو II by Riaz Hussain
# Memon - the Grade 2 book of the code ratified by the Sindhi Language Authority
# committee on 7 November 2016.  The letter and the word it stands for are read
# from the author's own manuscript; the braille is the Grade 1 cell for that
# letter, with the series prefix in front of it.
#
# The system has six series.  A contraction is the series prefix followed by one
# ordinary letter, and it stands for a whole word:
#
#   (no prefix)  a single letter standing alone as a word
#   dot 5        5-<letter>
#   dots 4 5     45-<letter>
#   dots 4 5 6   456-<letter>
#   dots 3 4 5 6 3456-<letter>
#   dot 6        6-<letter>
#
# and a seventh group, سنڌي اختصار, which abbreviates a phrase to its initial
# letters without any prefix.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS - READ THIS BEFORE USING
#
# FORWARD ONLY, and NOT YET CONFIRMED IN USE.
#
# What is certain: the contraction list itself.  Each entry pairs a word with a
# letter exactly as the author's manuscript pairs them.
#
# What is NOT yet established is when a contraction may be used.  Every Grade 2
# braille code has placement rules - whether a contraction may begin a word, end
# one, stand alone, or cross a syllable boundary - and those rules are not stated
# in the material available.  This table therefore applies every contraction as a
# WHOLE WORD ONLY (`word` rules), which is the conservative choice: it will miss
# contractions a human transcriber would make, but it will not make one that is
# wrong inside a word.
#
# The section نقطي چار پنج ڇهه is headed "ڪل ۽ جز لفظي" - whole AND partial word -
# so some of its entries are meant to apply inside a word too.  Which ones is a
# question for Riaz Hussain Memon.  Until he answers, they are whole-word here.
#
# Back-translation is not attempted.  Do not use this table with `-b`.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
include sd-pk-g1-core.uti

# ۾ has a contraction of its own here — the letter م, dots 134 — where Grade 1
# spells it out as م ي ن.  That is the whole reason the shared rules sit in
# sd-pk-g1-core.uti rather than in sd-pk-g1.utb: liblouis cannot override a
# rule that an include has already defined.
word \x06FE 134
noback always \x06FD 1-3-24-1345

